-- title:
--   Pic⁰ of the Igusa field generated by differences of chart points
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$, and the intermediate field $K$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly, and let $j \in K$ be a nonzero element whose Laurent series is the image of the $q$-expansion $j(q)$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and let $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension one and geometrically integral, together with closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ of $C_1$, $C_2$ over the base change to $k$ of the two-chart model $\mathrm{modelTo}\ A\ K\ j$, such that every point of that base change lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, the scheme-theoretic intersection $C_1 \times_X C_2$ is reduced, and its cardinality equals some $n > 0$. Let $w$ consist of a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with an integral power series realising its $q$-expansion whose reduction over $k$ is nonzero, let $\mathrm{Ig} =$ `igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w` be the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k$ generated over the function field of $X_1(M)$ by the inverse of that reduction, and let $\mathrm{Mdl}_2$ be a curve model of $\mathrm{Ig}$ over $k$ (an integral, proper, smooth relative dimension one curve with function field identified with $\mathrm{Ig}$, with a bijection between closed points and places) equipped with an isomorphism $e_2 : \mathrm{Mdl}_2.C \cong C_2$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$, and assume the preimage along $e_2$ followed by $i_2$ followed by the first projection of the open image of the $j$-finite chart is nonempty. Then for every finite set $S$ of places of $\mathrm{Ig}/k$ and every $x \in \mathrm{Pic}^0(\mathrm{Ig}/k)$, $x$ lies in the additive subgroup generated by those classes $\mathrm{Pic0.mk}$ of degree-zero divisors $\mathrm{single}(v)\,1 - \mathrm{single}(v')\,1$ for which $v, v'$ are the places attached by $\mathrm{Mdl}_2.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$ to $k$-points $c, c'$ of $C_2$ (sections of $c_2$, transported by $e_2^{-1}$) whose images avoid the range of the second projection of $C_1 \times_X C_2$, whose images in the two-chart model lie in the range of the $j$-finite chart $\mathrm{\iota Fin}\ A\ K\ j$, and with $v, v' \notin S$.
--
--   This is the generation step used to produce enough good points on the non-Gauss component of the special fibre: over an algebraically closed field the degree-zero divisor class group of a function field is generated by differences of places avoiding any prescribed finite set, here specialised to places coming from $k$-points of $C_2$ that lie off the crossings with $C_1$ and inside the $j$-finite chart. It is invoked in the construction of the Hecke-compatible comparison on the special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$.
